.\" man/man1/docv.1
.TH DOCV 1 2026-11-03 "docv 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
docv \- view manual pages and Markdown documents in a terminal, with fuzzy search
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY docv
.OP \-u
.YS
.
.SY docv
.OP \-u
.RI [ section ]
.I name
.YS
.
.SY docv
.OP \-u
.IB name ( section )
.YS
.
.SY docv
.OP \-u
.I file
.YS
.
.SY docv
.B path\-add
.IR dir \~...
.YS
.
.SY docv
.B path\-rm
.IR dir \~...
.YS
.
.SY docv
.B path\-list
.YS
.
.SY docv
.B gen\-cr
.OP \-o dir
.RI [ shard ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B docv
shows manual pages and Markdown documents in a full-screen terminal viewer.
It reads the roff source of a page itself, with the
.MR man 7
and
.MR mdoc 7
macro packages and
.MR tbl 1
tables built in, from plain or gzip-compressed files, and follows
.B .so
includes.
Files named
.IR *.md ,
.IR *.markdown ,
.IR *.mdown ,
.I *.mkd
or
.I *.mkdn
(optionally gzip-compressed) are read as Markdown instead (see
.BR MARKDOWN ).
.PP
The page is laid out to the width of the terminal, either wrapped or with
each paragraph on one line.
The page header of a manual page stays at the top of the screen and the
page footer at the bottom while the body scrolls between them.
Links can be followed and gone back from: cross-references such as
.MR ls 1 ,
and the links of a Markdown document to other files and to its headings.
Links to URLs are written as terminal hyperlinks (OSC 8).
A search bar fuzzy-finds in the displayed page, or in all pages of the
manual and the Markdown documents of the project.
Colors follow the terminal's own color theme.
.PP
A
.IR name ,
with an optional
.IR section ,
is looked up along the search path (see
.BR "SEARCH PATH" ).
A section prefix such as
.B 3
also matches
.B 3p
and
.BR 3type .
An argument that contains a slash, or names an existing file and is not a
section name, is read as a file: a page, or a Markdown document.
Without a page,
.B docv
opens on an empty page in the page search.
.PP
When standard output is not a terminal, the page is printed as plain text,
.B MANWIDTH
columns wide (80 when unset).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-unwrapped
Start in the unwrapped layout: one line per paragraph, scrolled sideways,
also when
.B start\-wrapped
in
.MR docv\-config 5
is true (the default).
Unfilled text and tables never wrap in either layout.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "path\-add " dir\~...
Add directories of man pages to the search path.
A directory is a tree of section directories
.RI ( man1/ ", " man3/ ", ...)"
or a directory with pages in it.
Each directory must exist; it is stored as an absolute path.
A directory without man pages is added with a warning.
.TP
.BI "path\-rm " dir\~...
Remove added directories.
Fails for a directory that was not added.
.TP
.B path\-list
Print the search path in order, each directory with where it comes from:
.BR project ,
.B added
or
.BR system .
.B (pages)
marks a directory with pages in it rather than a tree.
.TP
.BR "gen\-cr " [ \-o
.IR dir ]
.RI [ shard ]
Generate the man pages of a Crystal shard: the nearest directory from
.I shard
(the current directory by default) upward that holds a
.IR shard.yml .
It runs
.B crystal docs \-\-format json
there and renders
.I README.md
as the overview page
.IB name .7cr
and the doc comments of every type as
.IB Type .3cr
pages (with a
.IB name \-toplevel.3cr
page when the top level declares methods, macros or constants), into
.I dir
(default
.IR man ),
relative to the shard root.
The pages land in
.I man7/
and
.IR man3/ ,
so
.B docv
finds them as project pages.
A page whose content is unchanged keeps its file and date; generated pages
no longer produced are removed.
A file in the way that was not generated from doc comments stops the run.
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
sets the date of the pages.
.SH SEARCH PATH
Pages are looked up, and listed by the page search, along this path,
earlier directories first.
Within each tree, its locale subdirectories (from
.BR LC_ALL ,
.B LC_MESSAGES
or
.BR LANG )
come before it, and sections are searched in the order of
.BR man\-db .
.TP
.B The project around the current directory
The project root is the nearest directory upward that holds one of
.BR .git ,
.BR .hg ,
.BR .svn ,
.BR .jj ,
.BR shard.yml ,
.BR Cargo.toml ,
.BR package.json ,
.BR go.mod ,
.BR pyproject.toml ,
.BR setup.py ,
.BR Gemfile ,
.BR pom.xml ,
.BR build.gradle ,
.BR CMakeLists.txt ,
.BR meson.build ,
.B configure.ac
or a
.BR Makefile ,
looking no higher than below the home directory.
Without one, the current directory is the root, unless it is the home
directory or
.BR / .
The root and its subdirectories are searched four levels deep, skipping
hidden directories,
.BR node_modules ,
.BR vendor ,
.BR lib ,
.BR target ,
.B __pycache__
and symbolic links.
Trees of section directories
.RI ( man/man1/tool.1 )
and directories with pages in them
.RI ( doc/tool.1 ,
or the root itself) are taken.
A page there is a file named
.IB name . section\c
, optionally ending in
.BR .gz ,
whose text starts with a roff control character.
The Markdown documents found along the way, except hidden ones, are listed
by the page search too.
.TP
.B The added directories
From
.BR "docv path\-add" .
.TP
.B The system path
Built as
.MR man 1
builds it (see
.MR manpath 5 ):
.B MANPATH
when set, each empty component standing for the default path.
The default path takes, for each directory in
.BR PATH ,
its
.B MANPATH_MAP
directories from
.I /etc/man_db.conf
(or
.IR /etc/manpath.config ),
or else whichever of
.IR ../man ,
.IR man ,
.I ../share/man
and
.I share/man
exist next to it, and then the
.B MANDATORY_MANPATH
directories.
.SH SCREEN
The top row holds the title, the search bar between
.B \[u25D6]
and
.BR \[u25D7] ,
and a close mark
.RB ( \[u1F7AA] ).
A line runs below it.
Then comes the page, with the vertical scrollbar in the last column, of
which only the thumb
.RB ( \[u2503] )
is drawn, and below the page the horizontal scrollbar as a line, thumb
.B \[u2501]
on track
.BR \[u2500] .
The bottom row holds messages on the left, and on the right the layout, the
lines in view and the first column in view, for example
.RB \(lq "[wrap] \[u2502] 1\-56/801 \[u2502] col 1" \(rq.
While finding in the page it starts with the selected match and the number
of matches; while pages are listed it shows their count and the indexing
progress.
.SH KEYS
Keys are looked up by physical key first (the base layout key of the kitty
keyboard protocol), then by the key reported, then by the shifted symbol
without its shift, so
.B G
and
.B $
work on any keyboard layout.
.SS The page
.TP
.BR j ", " \(da ", " Ctrl\-n ", " Ctrl\-e
Line down.
.TP
.BR k ", " \(ua ", " Ctrl\-p ", " Ctrl\-y
Line up.
.TP
.BR Space ", " Ctrl\-f ", " PgDn
Page down.
.TP
.BR b ", " Ctrl\-b ", " Shift\-Space ", " PgUp
Page up.
.TP
.BR d ", " Ctrl\-d " / " u ", " Ctrl\-u
Half a page down / up.
.TP
.BR g ", " < ", " Home " / " G ", " > ", " End
Top / bottom.
.TP
.B l
Scroll right by 8 columns.
The arrow keys
.B \(<-
and
.B \(->
do not scroll.
.TP
.BR H " / " L
Scroll left / right by half a screen.
.TP
.BR 0 " / " $
Line start / line end.
.TP
.B w
Switch between the wrapped and the unwrapped layout.
.TP
.BR Tab " / " Shift\-Tab
Focus the next / previous link.
.TP
.B Enter
Follow the focused link (see
.BR LINKS ).
.TP
.BR Backspace ", " Alt\-\(<-
Back to the previous page.
.TP
.BR f ", " t
Focus the search bar to find in the page.
.TP
.BR / ", " o
Focus the search bar with
.B /
typed, to search the pages of the manual and the documents of the project.
.TP
.B h
Show the help: every key as it is bound, and the mouse gestures.
The scrolling keys and the wheel scroll it; any other key or a click closes
it.
.TP
.B Esc
Clear the link focus, the text selection and the message.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-l
Redraw the screen.
.TP
.BR q ", " Q ", " Ctrl\-c
Quit.
.SS The search bar
.TP
text
Type into the bar.
.TP
.B Enter
Stay at the selected match, or open the selected page.
.TP
.BR Esc ", " Ctrl\-c ", " Ctrl\-g
Leave the bar and empty it; when finding in the page, go back to where the
search started.
.TP
.B Backspace
Delete the last character.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-u
Clear the bar.
.TP
.BR \(da ", " Ctrl\-n ", " Tab " / " \(ua ", " Ctrl\-p ", " Shift\-Tab
Next / previous match or page.
.TP
.BR PgDn " / " PgUp
A screenful of matches or pages down / up.
.SH SEARCH BAR
Text without a leading
.B /
fuzzy-finds in the lines of the displayed page, in its current layout.
The page stays on screen: matched characters are highlighted in place, the
line of the selected match is shaded, and the page scrolls to the best match
while typing.
.PP
Text after a leading
.B /
lists the pages of the search path as
.IB name ( section )
with the description from their NAME section, and the Markdown documents of
the project by their path from the project root with their first heading
and paragraph, matched against both.
The project's pages and documents come first, also ahead of better matches
elsewhere.
A match in the name counts slightly more than an equal match in the
description, so
.B /list dir
finds
.MR ls 1
by its description.
The descriptions are read from the pages in the background while the list
is in use, and cached.
.PP
Matching is fuzzy: the characters of each space-separated term must appear
in order, and matches score higher at word starts, in runs of consecutive
characters and with short gaps.
Every term must match.
A term in lower case ignores case; a term with an upper-case letter matches
exactly.
Results are ranked best first within the project's entries and within the
others; ties go to the shorter name, then to section order.
.SH MOUSE
.TP
wheel
Scroll 3 lines.
.TP
.RB Shift\- "wheel, horizontal wheel"
Scroll 8 columns.
.TP
drag in the text
Select text; on release it is copied to the clipboard with OSC 52.
The selection stays highlighted until the next click or key.
Indentation and trailing blanks of a line are not selected, and the copied
lines lose the indentation they share: text comes out flush left, code keeps
its relative indentation.
.TP
double-click
Select the word under the pointer (letters, digits,
.B _
and
.BR \- )
or the run of punctuation, and copy it.
.TP
triple-click
Select the paragraph: the lines with text around the pointer in blocks of
the same kind (a heading alone), and copy it.
.TP
drag a thumb, click a track
Scroll; a click on a track pages in its direction.
.TP
click a link
Follow it.
.TP
click the search bar
Focus it.
.TP
hover over a listed page, click it
Highlight it, open it.
.TP
.RB "click " \[u1F7AA]
Quit.
.TP
back button
Back to the previous page.
.SH LINKS
A cross-reference
.IB name ( section )
in the text opens that page from the search path.
A Markdown link to a file opens the file, relative to the current one, at
the heading its
.BI # anchor
names; a link to
.BI # anchor
alone goes to that heading of the current document.
Anchors are GitHub's: the heading in lower case, punctuation dropped, spaces
as dashes, and
.BR \-1 ,
.BR \-2 ...
appended to repeated headings.
Following a link remembers the place, for
.BR Backspace .
.PP
A link to a URL (one with a scheme, such as
.B https:
or
.BR mailto: )
is written as a terminal hyperlink (OSC 8), for the terminal to open: most
terminals open it on a click with a modifier, such as
.B Ctrl\-Shift
in kitty, since the viewer itself takes plain clicks.
Following it in the viewer shows the URL.
.SH MARKDOWN
Markdown is read as CommonMark with the GitHub extensions: tables, task
lists, strikethrough, bare URLs as links, and alerts
.RB ( "> [!NOTE]" ).
Paragraphs fill to the width, list items hang on their bullet, number or
check box, block quotes get a bar
.RB ( \[u2502] )
per level, code blocks keep their lines unwrapped and indented, code spans
are never broken across lines, tables are
boxed as wide as the terminal with the header row ruled off, and horizontal
rules run across the width.
Headings keep their level, 1 to 6, each in its own color.
Raw HTML is dropped, keeping the text between the tags; an image shows its
description.
Markdown documents have no page header and footer.
.SH COLORS
Every element is drawn in a role, styled from the terminal's color theme.
On start, and again when the terminal reports a change of color scheme,
.B docv
asks the terminal for its colors with OSC 21 (the color control protocol of
.BR kitty ).
Once it answers, colors ramped toward its foreground or background, such as
the background of the search bar, are exact and drawn in 24-bit color.
Otherwise the standard xterm colors stand in, and the color depth comes from
.B COLORTERM
and
.BR TERM .
Colors a page sets itself are kept.
Roles are restyled in
.MR docv\-config 5 .
.SH TERMINAL
.B docv
switches to the alternate screen and uses the kitty keyboard protocol, SGR
mouse reports in pixels, in-band resize, focus, visibility and color scheme
notifications, synchronized updates, OSC 21 for the color theme, OSC 52
for the clipboard and OSC 8 for hyperlinks.
Terminals without some of these get the legacy key encodings, cell mouse
coordinates and default colors; the clipboard write first sends an invalid
payload, which clears the clipboard in terminals that append writes and is
ignored elsewhere.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MANPATH
The system search path; see
.BR "SEARCH PATH" .
.TP
.B PATH
The directories next to which the default system path looks for pages.
.TP
.B MANWIDTH
The width of plain text output.
.TP
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
The date, in seconds since the epoch, written into the pages
.B gen\-cr
generates, for reproducible builds; today when unset.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set and not empty, no colors at all: headings bold, arguments and links
underlined, selections in reverse video.
.TP
.B COLORTERM
.B truecolor
or
.B 24bit
selects 24-bit color.
.TP
.B TERM
A name ending in
.B \-direct
selects 24-bit color, one with
.B 256color
256 colors; otherwise the 16 ANSI colors.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
The base of the configuration directory,
.I ~/.config
when unset or not absolute.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
The base of the cache directory,
.I ~/.cache
when unset or not absolute.
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_MESSAGES ", " LANG
The locale whose page translations come first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docv/config.ini
The configuration, written with commented defaults on the first run; see
.MR docv\-config 5 .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docv/paths
The added directories, one per line; lines starting with
.B #
are comments.
.B path\-add
and
.B path\-rm
rewrite it.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/docv/index.tsv
The page descriptions of the page search.
A directory whose modification time is unchanged is read from it; in a
changed directory only files with a new modification time are read again.
The descriptions of the project's documents are read on every start.
.TP
.IR /etc/man_db.conf ", " /etc/manpath.config
The
.B man\-db
configuration read for the system path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
No such page, an unreadable page or document, an invalid configuration, a
failed
.BR gen\-cr ,
or a failed
.BR path\-add ,
.B path\-rm
or file write.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
docv ls
docv 3 printf
docv \(aqprintf(3)\(aq
docv ./doc/tool.1
docv README.md
docv \-u tar
docv path\-add ~/src/tool/man
docv gen\-cr && docv Foo::Bar
MANWIDTH=100 docv ls | less
.EE
